/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186305547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308020 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9e4bd274-b5ff-536c-adca-f46c1bdd94e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308404 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308404 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333184" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308404 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308404 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=6x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308404 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bf46b344-09be-5328-8704-8fe72b540c14" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308404 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=6$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=4$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis. Since ${e}^{6t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis. Since ${e}^{4t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, there are two phase portraits satisfying these conditions:\n\n![](images/24/2473117cdca4318187b94374820c0a12576e998e7f631a6e7bf51e56c985be43.png)\n\nLet's consider the solutions $x(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{6t}$ and $y(t)={c}_{2}{e}^{4t}$ provided that ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\ne 0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}=\\frac{({c}_{2}{e}^{4t})^{′}}{({c}_{1}{e}^{6t})^{′}}=\\frac{4{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}}{6{c}_{1}{e}^{6t}}=\\frac{2{c}_{2}}{3{c}_{1}}{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ meaning that the tangents to the solution become more and more horizontal as we move away from the origin. This corresponds to the following phase portrait:\n\n![](images/e8/e8110ea6d6a113e72e35502030afb495a23bc81106d64874582d03aae81b7c73.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308410 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333214" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308410 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308410 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below regarding the given decoupled system of linear differential equations.$\\,$\nThe $x$-axis is a {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-axis is a {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308410 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "59947953-f704-5cbc-beaf-56322b9434f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308410 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nRecall that a homogeneous system of linear differential equations has a single equilibrium (fixed point) at the origin.\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis and move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $x$-axis is the $\\text{unstable}$ line.\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $y$-axis is the $\\text{stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a saddle point}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/6d/6dc8ceb9a1c771f18d6e90d450cd837fe80c6bab7943ab7d397d90eb45754594.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391043 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391043 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332683" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391043 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391043 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-7y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391043 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3f7b6c7b-9bbd-58e1-9f4f-ab6d8faeb7f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391043 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-7$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-7t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis. Since ${e}^{2t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-7t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis. Since ${e}^{-7t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/d6/d604781deed3206caf0a3bf6afa857c00beca9d532a26dedef5c717b4f684225.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391044 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391044 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391044 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391044 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391044 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391044 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391044 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391044 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186391048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391044 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "23f7e5e5-ba46-5c75-bde7-3c2b00f02f16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391045 #edb/ref 1080 "images/7c/7c483bbf926df156b7f85fbedcbb6ab18571ff4f544416cd8ea554b70b59a589.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391045 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391045 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "50c7bc7d-0232-5fe1-a6d4-6f9a22440550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391046 #edb/ref 1080 "images/27/27c6bf8d11d3de50beac351f88104df58cac31053eb6ecfc3a35ce77ccd8600b.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391046 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391046 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9c4028ce-9f71-5bd4-ad6b-47272c4ba666" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391047 #edb/ref 1080 "images/01/01d93cb2e68123b061b057ce30b94bcce44401b2d0fc0c566b3c33478c07fb92.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391047 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391047 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f48f6682-16a0-5a4e-b948-d2adbb5ee402" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391048 #edb/ref 1080 "images/d6/d604781deed3206caf0a3bf6afa857c00beca9d532a26dedef5c717b4f684225.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391048 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391048 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4d70c978-6c43-538a-a72f-3e3d73db9a61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391049 #edb/ref 1080 "images/38/389d3cfc92ece3a63300767f92c34c11dccec981ac43f3f66a2ced02906f8a73.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391049 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391049 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e571bbe0-b813-51a0-a84b-7bcbc9e1fb37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391151 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391151 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333193" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391151 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391151 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391151 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "619ed97d-e84b-53da-afc0-cbcda9b4c479" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391151 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-4$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis. Since ${e}^{-3t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis. Since ${e}^{-4t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions also approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, there are two phase portraits satisfying these conditions:\n\n![](images/3f/3fdbeba46a0f4640e909b0ba489c1aec1fa87a6aa7740f19d08f274b7351d11b.png)\n\nLet's consider the solutions $x(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{-3t}$ and $y(t)={c}_{2}{e}^{-4t}$ provided that ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\ne 0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}=\\frac{({c}_{2}{e}^{-4t})^{′}}{({c}_{1}{e}^{-3t})^{′}}=\\frac{-4{c}_{2}{e}^{-4t}}{-3{c}_{1}{e}^{-3t}}=\\frac{4{c}_{2}}{3{c}_{1}}{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ meaning that the tangents to the solution become more and more horizontal as the trajectories approach the origin. This corresponds to the following phase portrait:\n\n![](images/41/4193300af5a8950ce70e2c469812424235665faac279dac0c89289a0307ab46a.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391152 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391152 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391152 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391152 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391152 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391152 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391152 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391152 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186391153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391152 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "69405513-1dbb-597a-8b25-1607c72536b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391153 #edb/ref 1080 "images/e8/e8e9a97ed196b5677e3c2ea6be32f4a1ab04f7721b3d9c41e4db284d69e6805a.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391153 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391153 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6009f5a2-68a9-5943-8731-39f000ed0199" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391154 #edb/ref 1080 "images/85/85cb5c01c72b8b903cc0b5fc8c593c0b6e96550380e6bc7af55d5db5b5f40d4e.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391154 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391154 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1b93024f-8207-52ad-845f-920de06ed5b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391155 #edb/ref 1080 "images/b4/b414b76f1fe20b5238e75281e57bb851c8e67777e225d7610631dab1b4921b82.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391155 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391155 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4a78d0da-5220-5127-8319-73b4acac217f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391156 #edb/ref 1080 "images/d1/d19a6d30c12f5d966578cd950db1f16a9bc309f3a24a8e2480e52edca1281f75.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391156 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391156 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c5cd3807-c498-5cde-99b9-07cd5a9bfab8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391157 #edb/ref 1080 "images/0c/0c70e2c185d054b8cc62411736ecec2e60a716d265819a82a171076d999ef4e6.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391157 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391157 #edb/